{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-boltzmann-constant","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:boltzmann-constant","kind":"definition","title":"Boltzmann constant in QOU natural units","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-quantum-temperature"],"tags":["boltzmann-constant","statistical-mechanics","planck-constant"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Information.thermalEnergy","text":"boltzmann-constant.md","leanSource":"boltzmann-constant.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:boltzmann-constant\"></a><p>In QOU natural units the <strong>Boltzmann constant</strong> is set to <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">k_B := 1</code>. With the quantum temperature <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T_q = \\hbar_q</code> of <a href=\"#def:quantum-temperature\" data-at=\"information-theory/stat-mech\">22.9.2</a>, the thermal energy is then</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  k_B \\, T_q = T_q = \\hbar_q = \\frac{q-1}{q}.</code></pre>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/boltzmann-constant.md","heading":"Definition","number":"22.9.10","page":"b/def-boltzmann-constant","qa":{"counts":{"pass":90,"fail":2,"warn":0,"na":14,"unknown":0,"stale":81},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.Information.thermalEnergy","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/boltzmann-constant.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
